  "id": "COMPOUND:26467 - PROTEIN:4992",
  "verbalization": "Decaturin B is implicated in the interaction with CWR22R through two distinct pathways. In the first pathway, Decaturin B targets Endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2, which in turn is a target of a complex compound, (16alpha,20R,24S)-16,24-epoxy-2,20,25-trihydroxycucurbita-1,5-diene-3,11,22-trione 2-O-beta-D-glucopyranoside, which ultimately targets CWR22R. In the second pathway, Decaturin B directly targets C-C motif chemokine 8, which is a target of Euphorbiaproliferin F, which also targets CWR22R. These two distinct pathways suggest that Decaturin B may influence CWR22R through different molecular mechanisms, potentially involving different cellular processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of Decaturin B's interaction with CWR22R, emphasizing the role of multiple targets in the regulation of this receptor.",
